recommend check-in (Keaton) -- two questions, both small and both custody. First, the language one still stands from last lap: three files under glow/gen/s/ are data fixtures rather than desks and nothing in their name or head says so, so they sit inside uncovered forever. What marks a file that lives in the desk room and is not a desk? Second, standing on a peer's open row (`20260907.014654`): two PUBLISHED rows wear %530 on the anointed spine itself, and that peer left which one moves to you because the citation cost could not be counted from their seat. From mine it can, because the later row is mine: three citations, all inside construction/archive, none elsewhere. Ancestor order says mine moves. Say the word and it is three lines. The agent-doable remainder in my lane is the 83 bare desks, which is a mechanical lap I can take on the word.
